              "isInner": false,
              "settings": {
                "html": "<section class=\"sec-editorial bg-img-hero text-center\">\n    <div class=\"overlay-layer overlay-emerald-pass\"></div>\n    <div class=\"container\" style=\"max-width: 950px;\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow-badge\" style=\"background: var(--emerald-bg); color: var(--emerald-pass); border-color: #86efac;\">THE REAL OPPORTUNITY</div>\n      <h2 class=\"sec-title\">Meanwhile, the <em>real</em> money on KDP was never in fragile AI novels anyway.</h2>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-body); text-align: left; line-height: 1.8;\">\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n          It's in <strong>low-content and puzzle books</strong> — word search, sudoku, mazes, coloring books, journals, planners, trackers, workbooks. Books that sell all year, need no \"prose,\" and can't be flagged as AI slop… because they're not slop. They're <em>structure.</em>\n        </p>\n        <p style=\"font-weight: 700; color: var(--blue-cobalt);\">\n          The catch? Making them well — with correct puzzles, verified answer keys, and files that actually pass KDP — is tedious, technical work. That's the wall 97% of people hit.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>",
                "_element_id": "section-10-the-real-opportunity"
